{
    "background_story": "Journi was a humble cell living in a bustling tissue. She spent her days surrounded by identical siblings, all working together to keep their host organism healthy. But Journi was special - she was a master of mitosis, the ancient art of cell division. With precision and speed, she could duplicate herself, creating identical copies that would grow and thrive. As the tissue grew and changed, Journi's mitotic abilities were in high demand. She worked tirelessly, dividing and multiplying, her descendants spreading throughout the tissue like a microscopic army. And yet, despite her importance, Journi remained humble, knowing that her true purpose was to serve the greater good of the organism. Her legacy lived on, a never-ending cycle of growth and renewal.",
